{"title":"Brushline Studio","sub":"Sign-ups are up 60%. Why isn't revenue?","type":"Growth strategy","industry":"Consumer software","geo":"Canada","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Cohort analysis · LTV vs CAC · channel economics","prompt":"Brushline makes a design app for small online sellers, at $12 a month. Last year it started buying ads on social media, and paying sign-ups rose 60%. But revenue grew much less than that, and cash is tight. The founder asks what's going on and what to do.","clarify":[{"q":"How do users arrive?","a":"Before the ads, almost all came through word of mouth, search and referrals. Now half come from social ads."},{"q":"Cost to acquire?","a":"About $40 per paying user through organic and referral marketing; about $90 through social ads."},{"q":"Margins?","a":"About 80% gross margin."}],"structure":{"root":"Is Brushline's growth profitable?","branches":[{"head":"Which users stay?","items":["Retention by acquisition channel"]},{"head":"What is a user worth?","items":["Months paid × $12 × margin"]},{"head":"What does a user cost?","items":["Acquisition cost by channel"]}]},"hypothesis":"Paid ads often bring users who try the app and leave. If they leave fast enough, each one costs more to acquire than they ever pay.","questions":[{"q":"Here is retention by channel. What do you see?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"398.836437pt\" height=\"191.004pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 398.836437 191.004\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 191.004 L 398.836437 191.004 L 398.836437 -0 L 0 -0 L 0 191.004 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 45.676437 165.896 L 391.636438 165.896 L 391.636438 27.296 L 45.676437 27.296 L 45.676437 165.896 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"m