3059 Q 1594 3059 1350 2892 Q 1107 2726 976 2422 Q 845 2118 845 1696 Q 845 1280 976 973 Q 1107 666 1350 502 Q 1594 339 1926 339 L 1926 339 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-2a\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(67 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(121.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-46\" transform=\"translate(145.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(205.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(227.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5e\" transform=\"translate(278.21875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-44\" transform=\"translate(338.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(392.328125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(416.234375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(471.03125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(494.9375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(516.34375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-46\" transform=\"translate(571.140625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(631.046875 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p3814e7b96c\"><rect x=\"45.676437\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · % of users still paying, by month since sign-up","note":null},"answer":"<p>Ad users drop off fast: only 45% are still paying in month 3 against 70% for organic users, and they keep cancelling faster after that (9% a month against 4%). By month 12, 48% of organic users remain vs 19% of ad users.</p>"},{"q":"Work out a user's lifetime value against the cost to acquire them, for each channel.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["Channel","Months paid","Lifetime gross profit ($)","Cost to acquire ($)","Value ÷ cost"],"rows":[["Organic and referral","19.3","185","40","4.64"],["Paid social ads","6.6","64","90","0.71"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Unit economics by channel","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p>Expected months paid = the first three months, then each later month at the channel's cancel rate: organic about <b>19.3 months</b>, ads about <b>6.6 months</b>.</p> <p>Lifetime gross profit = months × $12 × 80%: organic <b>$185</b>, ads <b>$64</b>.</p> <p>Against acquisition cost: organic 4.6× its $40 cost; ads <b>0.71×</b> its $90. <b>Each ad user loses about $26.</b></p>","note":"A common rule of thumb: value should be at least 3× the cost to acquire."},{"q":"What should the founder do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Cut social ad spend</b> sharply; keep only ad sets whose users retain like organic users</li> <li><b>Fix the first 3 months</b> for all users: onboarding templates, a first sale tracked in the app</li> <li><b>Put money into referrals</b>, the channel that works: a free month for both sides</li> <li>Track value ÷ cost by channel every month, not total sign-ups</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Brushline's ad-driven growth destroys value: ad users stay about 7 months against 19 for organic users, so each is worth about $64 of gross profit but costs $90 to acquire. I recommend cutting most social ad spend, investing in referrals (4.6× return), and improving the first three months to lift retention for every channel. Risk: sign-up growth will slow, so explain to investors why that is healthy. Next step: report retention and value ÷ cost by channel monthly.","great":["Reads cohort retention curves by channel","Turns retention into lifetime value","Compares lifetime value with acquisition cost","Recommends cutting a growth channel, with reasons"],"id":57,"slug":"brushline-studio"}